# Scripts that run inside Linux containers or a POSIX shell must keep LF line endings on every
# checkout. Without this, Windows clones with core.autocrlf=true silently convert them to CRLF,
# which breaks the shebang/`set` parsing the moment the file is bind-mounted into a container
# (bash reports "invalid option name" for an option like "pipefail\r").
*.sh text eol=lf

# C# sources for the same reason, with a sharper failure mode: several tests embed YAML in a raw
# string literal and compare it against "\n"-delimited text. Checked out as CRLF, those literals
# carry "\r\n", the comparison silently stops matching, and the test fails on Windows only.
*.cs text eol=lf
